1
00:00:00,695 --> 00:00:05,565
(Sheldon:)...where women and men of all races
and creeds work side by side as equals.

2
00:00:05,734 --> 00:00:09,864
(Leonard:)You mean where they were advanced
enough to invent an interstellar warp drive...

3
00:00:10,038 --> 00:00:13,368
(Leonard:)...but a black lady
still answered the space phone?

4
00:00:14,142 --> 00:00:17,942
(Howard:)Oh, I did spend a lot of my shower time
with Lieutenant Uhura.

5
00:00:20,115 --> 00:00:22,915
(Sheldon:)Howard's disturbing recollections aside...

6
00:00:23,385 --> 00:00:26,445
(Sheldon:)...I don't appreciate being forced
to do banal committee work.

7
00:00:26,621 --> 00:00:28,281
(Leonard:)I know. You're too smart for this.

8
00:00:28,457 --> 00:00:33,057
(Sheldon:)Exactly. It's like asking the Human Torch
to heat up your frozen burrito.

9
00:00:33,929 --> 00:00:38,059
(Leonard:)Got it. All right, I'm thinking one way
to counter bias in the peer-review process...

10
00:00:38,233 --> 00:00:41,393
(Leonard:)...is for papers to be submitted
under gender-neutral names...

11
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:43,630
(Leonard:)...like S. Smith instead of Samantha Smith.

12
00:00:43,805 --> 00:00:46,295
(Sheldon:)I suppose there is a history
of professional women...

13
00:00:46,475 --> 00:00:49,065
(Sheldon:)...using their initials
so as not to be pre-judged.

14
00:00:49,244 --> 00:00:53,574
(Sheldon:)Harry Potter's J.K. Rowling,
uh, Star Trek's D.C. Fontana.

15
00:00:53,748 --> 00:00:56,378
(Howard:)Van Nuys pole-dancer, D.D. Melons.

16
00:00:59,187 --> 00:01:02,817
(Howard:)All right. I think we've really helped
women today. Let's fire up the Xbox.

17
00:01:02,991 --> 00:01:06,521
(Leonard:)Don't make this a school project
where I'm the smart kid doing the work...

18
00:01:06,695 --> 00:01:08,595
...while the slackers sit and watch.

19
00:01:08,763 --> 00:01:11,293
We're not. You're the smart kid
doing all the work...

20
00:01:11,466 --> 00:01:13,936
(Sheldon:)...while the even smarter kids
sit back and watch.

21
00:01:15,137 --> 00:01:17,127
(Howard:)So you think I'm one of the smarter kids?

22
00:01:17,305 --> 00:01:21,025
(Sheldon:)No, you're a tool I was using
to make my point.

